 "replay_note": "A synthetic keydown (it moves nothing itself) stands for the PageDown, and window.scrollBy moves the page the captured distances. delayed: the key once the tour's panel has landed; all 675px 150ms after the tour's next step calls scrollIntoView, inside that step's own window (OWN_SCROLL_START_MS 400ms; the capture's arrived at 394ms). stalled: the key and the first 81px 900ms after step 1 scrolled (its own window over, so the 81px is seen as the visitor's, as in the capture), then the other 594px 150ms into step 2's own window. The stall is ~1.2s instead of the capture's ~230ms: the replay cannot place a piece between the panel's release and step 1 in WebKit (its frames run ~180ms apart under load), and a longer stall defeats any 'the visitor is at rest after N ms of stillness' rule just the same. Both replays assert the movement lands inside the step's window and within USER_INPUT_MS (1500ms) of the key."
